I continue telling Timo and Lena my story.
"In January I immediately took a taxi at the airport," I say.
"I gave the driver my new address."
"At the house I then paid for the trip."
Timo smiles and drinks some water.
"And then?" Lena asks curiously.
"Then I saw my new flat," I answer.
"But unfortunately the building has no elevator!"
"I pulled my heavy suitcase up the stairs."
Lena laughs out loud.
"I have often done that too," she says.
"On that first day I also met my neighbor," I tell them.
"I saw Sabine on the stairs."
"She has a small dog, his name is Bruno."
"Bruno found my suitcase very interesting right away."
Timo and Lena laugh at this picture.
I like my memories of January.
